@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Init Command
  "CLI handler for mason init that scaffolds a project .mason file."

  Provides:
    - cli.newInitCommand @source("symbol:newInitCommand")
    - cli.initDeps @source("symbol:initDeps")

  Consumes:
    - setup.InitProject
    - setup.DetectBuildDir
    - cli.defaultProvisionRun

  Invariants:
    - init MUST write .mason in the current directory and MUST refuse to overwrite an existing one
    - The URL MUST default to the folder name when it looks like a domain; the build folder MUST default to the detected one
    - Without -y init MUST prompt for URL and build folder (showing the defaults); with -y it MUST use the defaults and fail clearly when there is none
    - Unless --no-provision, init MUST offer to provision the new site using the file it just wrote; a provisioning failure MUST NOT remove the file

  OutOfScope:
    - Interactive setup wizard (future M-070)

  Scenario (happy-path): Init project
    Given no existing .mason
    When init runs
    Then it reports the created config path

  Scenario (negative): Existing config
    Given .mason already exists
    When init runs
    Then it returns an error
